            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>Q1: What is the cheapest time to fly from Chicago to Greece?</h3>
            <p>The cheapest fares are found during the off-season months of January and February, with round-trip economy tickets often available for $600-$900. For summer travel, book 40-60 days in advance and consider shoulder season months like May or September for the best balance of price and weather. Tuesday and Wednesday departures are consistently cheaper than weekend flights.</p>

            <h3>Q2: Are there direct flights from Chicago to Greece?</h3>
            <p>Yes, both United Airlines and American Airlines operate seasonal nonstop flights from Chicago O'Hare to Athens during the summer months, typically from May through October. These flights take approximately 10 hours and 15 minutes. Outside this period, all flights require at least one connection through European or Middle Eastern hubs like Frankfurt, Munich, London, or Istanbul.</p>

            <h3>Q3: Do I need a visa to visit Greece from the US?</h3>
            <p>No, US citizens do not need a visa for short tourist stays in Greece. You can stay up to 90 days within any 180 days under the Schengen Area visa-free rules. You will need a valid passport with at least three months' validity beyond your planned departure date from Greece. No additional documentation is required for standard tourism visits.</p>

            <h3>Q4: How much baggage can I bring on a Chicago to Greece flight?</h3>
            <p>Most full-service airlines allow one free checked bag up to 50 lbs (23 kg) and one carry-on bag plus a personal item on international flights between Chicago and Greece. Premium cabin and elite status passengers may bring additional bags. Low-cost carriers and basic economy fares may charge for checked baggage. Always verify your specific airline's policy before packing.</p>

            <h3>Q5: What is the best way to get from Athens Airport to the city center?</h3>
            <p>The Metro Line 3 is the most affordable and reliable option, reaching central Athens in about 40 minutes for approximately €9. Official airport taxis offer door-to-door service for a fixed fare of €40during the day or €55 at night. Airport express buses serve key locations including Syntagma Square and Piraeus Port. For groups or those with heavy luggage, pre-booked private transfers provide convenience at a moderate premium.</p>




